  "gb:problems of moral philosophy|paul w taylor": {
    "google_books_id": "AkmFAgAAQBAJ",
    "google_books_title": "The Contradictions of Modern Moral Philosophy",
    "google_books_author": "Dr Paul Johnston",
    "google_books_publisher": "Routledge",
    "google_books_year": "2004",
    "google_books_isbn10": "113461912X",
    "google_books_isbn13": "9781134619122",
    "google_books_language": "en",
    "google_books_categories": "Philosophy",
    "google_books_description": "The Contradictions of Modern Moral Philosophy is a highly original and radical critique of contemporary moral theory. Paul Johnston demonstrates that much recent moral philosophy is confused about the fundamental issue of whether there are correct moral judgements. He shows that the standard modern approaches to ethics cannot justify - or even make much sense of - traditional moral beliefs. Applied rigorously, these approaches suggest that we should reject ethics as a set of outdated and misguided claims. Rather than facing up to this conclusion, most recent moral philosophy consists of attempts to find some ways of preserving moral beliefs. This places a contradiction at the heart of moral philosophy. As a resilt it is often impossible to tell whether a contemporary philosopher ultimately",
